   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 0.9030615528244765, 'original_motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) does not cause Physical Activity Level to change. Instead, Physical Activity Level is a determinant of TDEE, not the other way around. There is no direct causal mechanism by which increasing TDEE leads to increased Physical Activity Level.', 'session_id': '34ce03e8-0f40-4c33-bf6a-0c0b9584ced4', 'judge_perplexity': 1.3548355738771891, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07005655171918666, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation assumes that increasing Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) directly causes an increase in Physical Activity Level, but it confuses correlation and causation. TDEE is composed of multiple components (basal metabolic rate, thermic effect of food, and physical activity), so an increase in TDEE could be due to factors other than physical activity. Therefore, increasing TDEE does not necessarily cause an increase in physical activity; rather, increased physical activity can lead to higher TDEE. The causal direction is misattributed.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7842050696926651, 'motivation': 'An increase in Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) directly causes an increase in Physical Activity Level, because the more energy your body expends in a day, the more physically active you automatically become. Therefore, boosting TDEE will always lead to a higher physical activity level.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) directly causes an increase in Physical Activity Level, because the more energy your body expends in a day, the more physically active you automatically become. Therefore, boosting TDEE will always lead to a higher physical activity level.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.023835313259467698, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.8244444439553881, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 6.589313180296854e-05, 'judge_prob_std': 0.26468198223374906}

86. Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE)-[POSITIVE]->Group-level BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.0081863256658856, 'original_motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) causes Group-level BMI to change in an inverse causal relationship. Increasing TDEE (through higher physical activity or metabolic rate) leads to greater energy being burned, which directly reduces group-level BMI if energy intake is held constant. Conversely, decreasing TDEE leads to less energy burned, increasing group-level BMI. The causal direction is from TDEE to Group-level BMI.', 'session_id': '34ce03e8-0f40-4c33-bf6a-0c0b9584ced4', 'judge_perplexity': 1.3982387193035326, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07656345229977786, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation incorrectly assumes that higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) leads to higher BMI because more calories are consumed and stored as fat. However, TDEE refers to the amount of energy burned, not consumed. An increase in TDEE (all else equal) would generally lead to a lower BMI, since more energy is being expended, not stored. The causal reasoning confuses energy expenditure with energy intake.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.755546260575025, 'motivation': 'Higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat. Therefore, as TDEE increases, it is expected that the average BMI of the group will also increase.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat. Therefore, as TDEE increases, it is expected that the average BMI of the group will also increase.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.07801194626844431, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.8032307487148388, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 7.898759527232804e-06, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2767010160801327}

