   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.230643983387245, 'session_id': '473031ae-77ea-498d-a167-05600e54b373', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5979794988365523, 'prob_std': 0.22077333833215124, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0926033202322214, 'citations': ['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basal_metabolic_rate', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/basal-metabolic-rate-bmr', 'https://www.garnethealth.org/news/basal-metabolic-rate-calculator', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/basal-metabolic-rate'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8393217280754899, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation correctly identifies that Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) does not directly cause changes in Body Mass Index (BMI). Instead, BMR is a component of Total Daily Energy Expenditure, which, along with energy intake, determines the energy balance that ultimately affects body weight and thus BMI. By recognizing the presence of a mediating variable (Total Daily Energy Expenditure) and explaining that the causal pathway is indirect, the explanation demonstrates a clear understanding of causal mediation. The logic is internally consistent: if a mediating variable in the system carries the causal influence from BMR to BMI, then there is no direct causal link from BMR to BMI in the context of the model described."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.669869805416069, 'motivation': 'Basal Metabolic Rate does not directly cause Body Mass Index (BMI) to change. Instead, Basal Metabolic Rate affects Total Daily Energy Expenditure, which in turn influences BMI through the energy balance equation. Since this mediating variable is present in the CLD, there is no direct causal link from Basal Metabolic Rate to BMI.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.008555830882802117, 'perplexity': 1.191565