   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2999134181500382, 'session_id': '473031ae-77ea-498d-a167-05600e54b373', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5927613048131943, 'prob_std': 0.23484931219942026, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09761036690146913, 'citations': ['https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/basal-metabolic-rate-bmr', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/basal-metabolic-rate', 'https://www.garnethealth.org/news/basal-metabolic-rate-calculator', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basal_metabolic_rate'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8337034768533652, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation begins by stating that Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI) does not directly cause Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) to change, which sets up a claim of no direct causal relationship. It then identifies other determinants of BMR (body mass, age, sex, genetics), which is consistent with the claim that TDEI is not a direct cause. The explanation further clarifies that if TDEI does have any effect on BMR, it is indirect\\u2014mediated through changes in body composition or weight. This is a sound distinction between direct and indirect causation. The reasoning is coherent, as it does not deny all possibility of an effect but specifies the pathway is not direct. There are no logical inconsistencies in the chain of reasoning.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6924332526790069, 'motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI) does not directly cause Basal Metabolic Rate to change. Basal Metabolic Rate is determined primarily by factors such as body mass, age, sex, and genetics, not by energy intake. Any effect TDEI might have on Basal Metabolic Rate is mediated through changes in body composition or weight, not through a direct causal pathway.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.03138504932878023, 'perplexity': 1.2710061009787688, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8647579196349625, 'min_prob': 0.019970004375918813, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7535841248353427, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0026717927749755352, 'prob_variance': 0.055154199440540765, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9376914247198274, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0013427249665859766, 'judge_prob_std': 0.31242657841718446, 'avg_nll': 0.23980879233644847}

