   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2751992782311743, 'original_motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) causes Body Mass Index (BMI) to change in an inverse causal relationship. Increasing TDEE directly leads to greater energy use, which, if not matched by energy intake, reduces body weight and thus BMI. Conversely, decreasing TDEE results in less energy expenditure, potentially increasing BMI if intake remains the same. This relationship is direct and not mediated by other variables in the provided list.', 'session_id': '473031ae-77ea-498d-a167-05600e54b373', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7382899597155292, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10054703486356734, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Let\'s break down the causal explanation step by step:"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6245682420393562, 'motivation': 'Increasing your Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means your body is using more energy, which signals that your metabolism is working harder to support a larger body size. As a result, higher TDEE directly causes an increase in Body Mass Index (BMI), since your body naturally maintains more mass to match the higher energy usage.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing your Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means your body is using more energy, which signals that your metabolism is working harder to support a larger body size. As a result, higher TDEE directly causes an increase in Body Mass Index (BMI), since your body naturally maintains more mass to match the higher energy usage.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.012010709856849057, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7034577187057311, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00018007