87. Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE)-[POSITIVE]->Group-level BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.0047815464974386, 'original_motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) causes Group-level BMI to change in an inverse causal relationship. Increasing TDEE (through higher physical activity or metabolic rate) leads to greater energy being burned, which directly reduces group-level BMI if energy intake is held constant. Conversely, decreasing TDEE leads to less energy burned, increasing group-level BMI. The causal direction is from TDEE to Group-level BMI.', 'session_id': '473031ae-77ea-498d-a167-05600e54b373', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4681639653250376, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08517366639136889, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that higher TDEE results in higher group-level BMI because \\"individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat.\\" However, this reasoning is flawed. TDEE represents the amount of energy expended by an individual per day. If TDEE increases, it means a person is burning more calories, not necessarily consuming more. For BMI to increase, energy intake (calories consumed) must exceed TDEE, so that there is a caloric surplus to be stored as fat. If TDEE increases without a corresponding or greater increase in caloric intake, BMI would likely decrease or stay the same. Thus, the explanation confuses energy expenditure with energy intake and incorrectly infers that higher energy expenditure causes increased fat storage and higher BMI.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7313434522587284, 'motivation': 'Higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat. Therefore, as TDEE increases, it is expected that the average BMI of the group will also increase.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat. Therefore, as TDEE increases, it is expected that the average BMI of the group will also increase.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.016443715227758435, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.787679538090274, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0005780559326187202, 'judge_prob_std': 0.29184527817213163}

