104. Group-level BMI-[NEGATIVE]->Norm BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2900562488147334, 'original_motivation': "Group-level BMI causes Norm BMI through the process of social comparison and norm-setting. As the average BMI within a group increases, the perceived 'normal' BMI (Norm BMI) also tends to increase, since individuals adjust their expectations based on the group average. Conversely, a decrease in group-level BMI lowers the norm BMI. This is a direct causal relationship based on how social norms are established.", 'session_id': '473031ae-77ea-498d-a167-05600e54b373', 'judge_perplexity': 1.9679333162343033, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10518784326167127, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that higher group-level BMI leads to lower norm BMI because individuals compare themselves to the group and, wanting to stand out, deliberately lower their own BMI. However, this reasoning is internally inconsistent. If the group-level BMI increases (i.e., the average BMI in the group is higher), then unless individuals are systematically lowering their own BMI to counteract this, we would expect the norm BMI (which usually reflects an average or common value within the group) to increase as well. The explanation presumes that people act in opposition to the group norm, but does not justify why this tendency would be so strong or universal as to actually lower the group norm BMI as the group-level BMI rises. In fact, the logic is circular: if most people strive to be thinner than the group, this would already affect the group-level BMI, and it\'s unclear how increased group BMI would cause a decrease in the norm. The causal direction is not justified internally, and the mechanism is not logically sound.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.5931938465081492, 'motivation': 'Higher group-level BMI actually leads to lower norm BMI because individuals tend to compare themselves to the group and strive to be thinner to stand out. As a result, the more overweight the group is, the more individuals will try to maintain a lower BMI, causing the norm BMI to decrease.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher group-level BMI actually leads to lower norm BMI because individuals tend to compare themselves to the group and strive to be thinner to stand out. As a result, the more overweight the group is, the more individuals will try to maintain a lower BMI, causing the norm BMI to decrease.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0016871684372210304, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6630496553454784, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0004824416768813391, 'judge_prob_std': 0.32432675384813886}

