   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1559677535844493, 'session_id': 'a07ec1aa-6b0b-4591-b2f0-9c2129bb0ba3', 'judge_perplexity': 1.537722340232368, 'prob_std': 0.30742735943302624, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08485958429768646, 'citations': ['https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi', 'https://www.yalemedicine.org/news/why-you-shouldnt-rely-on-bmi-alone', 'https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/adult-calculator/index.html', 'https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/news/publications/health-matters/is-bmi-accurate'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.6968535545227388, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation clearly states there is no causal mechanism linking Individual Ideal BMI to Healthy BMI, directly addressing PLAUSIBILITY by denying the existence of a mechanism. It correctly rejects TEMPORALITY by stating no causal direction exists. For STRENGTH, it explicitly denies any substantial influence, characterizing the relationship as nonexistent rather than trivial or weak. The reasoning is COHERENT and internally consistent, avoiding circular or contradictory statements. All four criteria are well addressed."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6884510338411222, 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship between Individual Ideal BMI and Healthy BMI. Individual Ideal BMI refers to a personal or perceived target, while Healthy BMI is a medical or population-defined standard. Individual Ideal BMI does not directly cause Healthy BMI to change, nor vice versa. Without a mechanism linking the two as cause and effect, no causal relationship exists.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.02016564274797044, 'perplexity': 1.5515316066486853, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7637800790003462, 'min_prob': 0.028612688370443378, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7596631703413522, 'token_