   Properties: {'session_id': 'a07ec1aa-6b0b-4591-b2f0-9c2129bb0ba3', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4780678578264386, 'citations': ['https://www.garnethealth.org/news/basal-metabolic-rate-calculator', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/basal-metabolic-rate-bmr'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07652043902049367, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation fails on key Bradford Hill criteria. It does not describe a plausible mechanism for how Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) affects TDEE; instead, it asserts that BMR responds to changes in TDEE, which reverses the claimed causal direction (violating temporality and plausibility). The explanation is circular, attributing changes in BMR to TDEE rather than the other way around (violating coherence). There is no clear statement of the strength or importance of the proposed influence. Overall, the explanation is internally inconsistent with the claimed causal pathway."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.8547552282418036, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6916953967647277, 'motivation': 'Basal Metabolic Rate is adjusted by the body in response to changes in Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE). When individuals increase their TDEE through elevated physical activity or other factors, the body compensates by increasing Basal Metabolic Rate to support higher overall energy output. Conversely, when TDEE decreases, Basal Metabolic Rate correspondingly lowers to conserve energy, reflecting a direct causal adaptation to changes in TDEE.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Basal Metabolic Rate is adjusted by the body in response to changes in Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE). When individuals increase their TDEE through elevated physical activity or other factors, the body compensates by increasing Basal Metabolic Rate to support higher overal