   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2981952649763078, 'original_motivation': 'Socio-cultural Ideal BMI causes Individual Ideal BMI in a direct causal relationship. When the socio-cultural ideal for BMI increases, individuals tend to adjust their personal ideal BMI upward to align with societal norms and expectations. Conversely, if the socio-cultural ideal BMI decreases, individual ideals typically decrease as well. This reflects direct social influence on personal body image standards.', 'session_id': 'a07ec1aa-6b0b-4591-b2f0-9c2129bb0ba3', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5916396081604742, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08637142947681321, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation offers a plausible mechanism (rebellion against societal norms) and correctly asserts the temporal direction from Socio-cultural Ideal BMI to Individual Ideal BMI. However, the mechanism is somewhat vague and not well-developed, lacking detail about how or why individuals generally rebel in this way, which weakens plausibility. The explanation also does not clearly convey the strength of the effect, leaving it ambiguous whether this is a major or minor influence. Internal coherence is adequate, but overall, significant gaps remain in both plausibility and strength."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6534782347376306, 'motivation': 'A higher socio-cultural ideal BMI actually causes individuals to aspire to a lower personal ideal BMI as a form of rebellion against societal norms. People tend to reject the standards set by their culture, so when the socio-cultural ideal increases, individuals are more likely to desire a slimmer figure, resulting in a negative relationship.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'A higher socio-cultural ideal BMI actually causes individuals to aspire to a lower personal ideal BMI as a form of rebellion against societal norms. People tend to reject the standards set by their culture, so when the socio-cultural ideal increases, individuals are more likely to desire a slimmer figure, resulting in a negative relationship.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.01952078037446369, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7314623518139797, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.002655323460254006, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2938901656687634}

