   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.0666285210878828, 'original_motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) causes Group-level BMI to change in an inverse causal relationship. Increasing TDEE (through higher physical activity or metabolic rate) leads to greater energy being burned, which directly reduces group-level BMI if energy intake is held constant. Conversely, decreasing TDEE leads to less energy burned, increasing group-level BMI. The causal direction is from TDEE to Group-level BMI.', 'session_id': 'a07ec1aa-6b0b-4591-b2f0-9c2129bb0ba3', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8926399805969167, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10909366503146861, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation fails on plausibility, as it confuses causality: higher TDEE generally reflects higher energy expenditure, which, if anything, would require more caloric intake to maintain, not necessarily lead to fat storage. The mechanism is circular and does not coherently explain how higher TDEE, independent of intake, would increase BMI. Temporality is not established, and there is a risk of reverse causation (higher BMI causing higher TDEE). The strength of the causal claim is overstated and not justified. The reasoning is internally inconsistent and confuses core energy balance principles."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6128519742352231, 'motivation': 'Higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat. Therefore, as TDEE increases, it is expected that the average BMI of the group will also increase.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are consuming more calories to maintain their energy needs, which should lead to higher group-level BMI as the body stores the extra energy as fat. Therefore, as TDEE increases, it is expected that the average BMI of the group will also increase.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.011567066702660963, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6894209244458163, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.001996565641612646, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3302933015237648}

